      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IAMTHEDEVILSELBOW (1) looks ready to break through after another solid effort at Bordertown, where he raced on speed before weakening late into fifth over 1550m. This is a suitable assignment and with 2kg less to carry here, he looks the one to beat. PEYTON JANE (6) got a long way out of her ground before finishing sixth at Naracoorte. She needs to improve, but with a cleaner run on he home track, she can figure in the finish at odds. RESILIENT RUBY (7) was well beaten at Naracoorte last time after racing too keenly early on, but her previous sixth at Murray Bridge was much more encouraging, and she can give this a shake. TAAJWAR (2) drops in grade from his last run, and he is back on his home track. Include in all top 4 combos to be safe.",
